@format 1
@id queue.clear-tabs
@title Clear all tab contents
@area 4. Queue and scheduling
@entry input
@summary Confirm the command, clear viewer, file-list, and group state in every tab, and show why section state is cleared only for the active workspace.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related files.clear, preview.close-media, split.section-delete

@alias console = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PConsole
@alias tabset = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.LTabset
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList
@alias group = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PGroup
@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow

[input] Clear Tabs requested <input>
- Receive the Clear Tabs command @ console.PConsoleTabsHandle(...)
> confirm

[confirm] Confirm removal <decision>
- Apply the destructive-action confirmation preference @ console.PConsoleDestructiveConfirm(...)
? "Clearing is declined" > unchanged
? "Clearing proceeds" > clear

[clear] Clear each tab container <process>
- Force-close the tab viewer when media is loaded @ tabset.LTabsetContentClear(...)
- Clear every non-empty file list @ list.PListClear(...)
- Clear every merge group container @ group.PGroupClear(...)
- Raise an empty-media notification from each viewer that was closed @ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
> active

[active] Is this the active workspace? <decision>
- The window subscribes its media handler only to the currently attached viewer @ window.PWindowWorkspaceAttach(...)
? "Viewer belongs to active workspace" > flow-clear
? "Viewer belongs to inactive workspace" > retained

[flow-clear] Clear active timeline state <process>
- Receive the empty-media notification for the active viewer @ window.PWindowMediaHandle(...)
- Clear the active flow source, spool, cursor, sections, keyframes, and waveform @ flow.PFlowClear(...)
> complete

[retained] Inactive flow receives no clear event <error>
- Leave the inactive workspace flow untouched because its viewer is not subscribed to the window media handler @ window.PWindowWorkspaceDetach(...)
> complete

[complete] Tab clearing finishes <output>
= Viewer, file-list, and group state is cleared across tabs, but an inactive tab can retain its section list after its media has been unloaded.

[unchanged] Tabs unchanged <output>
= No tab content is cleared.
